{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "So Much to Do at Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The New Assignment"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Discuss factual and abstract information about common everyday or job related topics in both work and social contexts appropriate for the interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Perfect Infinitives After <span class=\"italic\">Seem</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Appear</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use any perfect tense to talk about an action that is already completed. They connect past actions to current situations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ordinary infinitives usually talk about the present or future time periods.<br/> You use perfect infinitives (to have + past participle) after linking verbs like <span class=\"italic\">seem</span> and <span class=\"italic\">appear to</span> talk about a previous time period. <br/><br/>   For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">There <span class=\"strong\">seems to have been</span> some sort of mistake.<br/> There <span class=\"strong\">appears to have been</span> an error in the report.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It seems like we've been swamped with work this month."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It seems you have forgotten how fast things move around here."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There seems to have been a mix-up."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The matter appears to have been resolved. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "book jacket "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a paper cover of a book which you can remove"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Each of you will be writing copy for a book jacket. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to describe an assignment."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "flap"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a thin flat piece of paper that is attached to a surface, which you can lift up easily"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The outer cover has folded flaps. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "author bio "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a short piece of writing about the life of someone who has written a book"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The back cover is the one which will be printed with the author's bio."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "blurb"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a short description giving information about something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You'll be including a blurb on the back cover as well."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "critical praise "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "positive reviews about something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There will be puffs of critical praise."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reviewer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who writes about a new book in a newspaper or magazine "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The critical praise will come up from reviewers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "soft copy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "information shown on a screen rather than printed on paper"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You'll receive a soft copy of the assignment."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob01aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "word count"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the number of words in a document "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Is there a word count for this document?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob01aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le12ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go to the library."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find 3-5 books of different genres with book jackets. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Identify the different parts of it. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "What are the differences between the books? The genres? Look for examples of the Future Continous tense on the jackets. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down your findings. Present them to a partner. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read and identify the different elements of a book jacket. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I identify sentences about expectations in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk to a partner about the differences in book jackets."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Future Continuous and Stative Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Stative verbs are verbs that describe states that stay the same instead of actions or events that change. The most common stative verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You do not normally use stative verbs in the Future Continuous tense. <br/><br/>  Some examples of stative verbs are: <span class=\"italic\">love</span>, <span class=\"italic\">doubt</span>, <span class=\"italic\">care</span>, <span class=\"italic\">believe</span>, <span class=\"italic\">remember</span>.<br/><br/>  You can use some stative verbs with the Future Continuous tense. <br/> Look at the chart for a list of the kinds of stative verbs you can use:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Rule\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" when they have an active meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will be tasting</span> a variety of wines.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" when they emphasize change or development\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ll be including</span> a blurb and puffs of critical praise.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" when they involve a change in meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ll be thinking</span> about it later.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" when they refer to physical feelings\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">My head <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will be aching</span> by the end of the day.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll be expecting you to complete this task properly this time around."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You'll be getting a feel for the tight deadlines."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You'll be realizing pretty quickly that there isn't much space."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le12ob01re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le12ob01re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le12ob01re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Adam, Kristi. I have a new assignment for you both.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: We just finished up with one!<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Yes, Mr.Bari. I'll be expecting you to complete this task properly this time around.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: What's the task?\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Each of you will be writing copy for a book jacket.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Cool!", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le12ob01re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: The outer cover has folded flaps. You will be completing the flaps initially. The back cover is the one which will be printed with the author's bio. You'll be including a blurb and puffs of critical praise from reviewers on the back cover. You'll be both receiving a soft copy of the jacket.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: How long will we have to complete all this?<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: You'll be getting a feel for the tight deadlines involved in this industry. You have 2 days.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: That's it, 2 working days? It seems like we've been swamped with work this month.<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Yes, Mr. Bari. It seems you have forgotten how fast things move in the publishing world.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I have a question, is there a word count?", "id": 2, "time": "15000", "image": "engenn10le12ob01re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: You'll be realizing pretty quickly that there isn't much space and that every word counts. There are only about 150 words that'll be appearing on the back cover and they will arguably be the most important words in the entire book. After the title, the back cover appears to be what readers have looked at when deciding whether to make a purchase. Think of it as an ad.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Okay.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Any more questions? Adam?<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: No. However, there's an issue. There seems to have been a mix-up \u2026 I think.<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Please be more specific.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I'm looking at the e-mail that has a copy of the book jacket attached. This is for a children's book.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Yeah, I see it too. Aren't we're working with a memoir?<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Hmmm \u2026 aha! The matter appears to have been resolved.", "id": 3, "time": "56500", "image": "engenn10le12ob01re2img07.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about an unusual or unique event related to work topics."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can request or report facts about events or actions related to work issues."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about expectations for the future."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What was the last assignment you had to do in your job?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What was it about?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "What's the new assignment abou